We've been running with the Pack Leashes hands-free leash for about a month now. Here's the honest version.

## What we tested

The hands-free bungee leash. Remy's 70 lbs of pure pull, so this thing got a real workout on morning trail runs and regular neighborhood walks.

## What worked

The bungee absorbed most of Remy's lunges without yanking my hip. That matters a lot at 6am when you're half asleep. The waist clip stayed put even on longer runs, and the quick-release worked exactly how it should when we passed other dogs.

Material feels solid. Not flimsy. The hardware looks like it'll actually hold up.

## What didn't work

The leash length is fixed, which is fine for running but a little short when you want to give the dog some slack to sniff around. For trail running it's great. For a casual stroll, you might want more room.

Also took a few tries to get the waist fit dialed in right. Not a big deal, just worth knowing.

## Remy's take

Approved. He didn't chew it, which is honestly the highest honor he can give.

